# gofmt emits LF and only LF, so the formatting gate in .golangci.yml can only
# be checked against an LF working tree — on a CRLF checkout every file reports
# as unformatted and the gate is useless locally. That is the reason this file
# exists; the rest follows from the same place, since everything CI runs, it
# runs on Linux or inside a container: the shell scripts under scripts/, the
# Dockerfiles and nginx/Caddy configs under test/integration/, the Python
# gates. A CRLF shebang line is a container-only failure that no local run
# reproduces.
#
# eol=lf on the catch-all rather than per-extension: the per-extension form is
# what a new file type quietly falls through. text=auto still keeps git's
# binary detection, and the one committed binary is pinned below.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pyc binary
